      "id": "intro",
      "type": "title",
      "narration": "Prices rose almost every year, but never at the same speed. This is the story of how fast they climbed, measured December to December, from twenty sixteen through twenty twenty three.",
      "props": {
        "headline": "How fast prices rose",
        "kicker": "US INFLATION"
      },
      "cues": []
    },
    {
      "id": "trend",
      "type": "line-chart",
      "narration": "From twenty sixteen through twenty nineteen, yearly inflation hovered near two percent. Then came twenty twenty one. It jumped sharply, hit its high mark, and then began falling again.",
